<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Cleartext (http://) traffic is allowed for two reasons:

    1. Mockonomy's OWN loopback requests. The "Test connection" diagnostics send a
       request to the running server over 127.0.0.1; without this permission the app
       itself hits the same cleartext block as the app the user is testing, and the
       diagnostics wrongly report "the server did not respond" (seen on a device).

    2. The proxy target. Unmatched requests are forwarded to the target the user
       configured; internal staging servers often speak http://. Since the target is an
       arbitrary user URL, it cannot be limited with a domain list — cleartext must be
       allowed in base-config, otherwise the proxy fails silently.

    Security note: this permission does not widen the traffic Mockonomy produces. The app
    only talks to the loopback mock server and to the proxy target the user chose; there
    are no other outgoing connections.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
